From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:27:33 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 50/76] flashnext cuda: the --tp 2 prompt exchange sends only
 the half rows each rank owns

At --tp 2 each rank holds whole routed experts, and the shared expert's columns in halves (or whole on rank 0), so
every half row of a pair's slot in y is non-zero on one rank only. A prompt pass's reduce-scatter still moved all
eleven slots of the peer's rows, 110 KiB a row.

- fn_owner_rows, right after routing: each block's half rows both ways as prefix sums, copied to the host while the
  experts run.
- After the experts, in rounds that fit the spent expert activations: fn_owner_pack packs this rank's half rows for
  the peer's rows, one NCCL send and receive swaps them (received into the peer's rows of y, already packed), and
  fn_owner_sum sums this rank's rows as fn_moe_sum does, each value plus 0 as the reduce-scatter left it.
- The sums gather is unchanged, so every sum keeps TP1's order and bits. A captured pass keeps the reduce-scatter.
